@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk Non Integration
	Testing updates that should not be present in Zendesk caused by changes in OSB.

Setup:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	* I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I create a project with the following values
	| Name         | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Code         | ZENOSBA            |
	| Type         | Group              |
	| Industry     | Automotive         |
	| Tier         | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts | 10                 |
	| Address Line | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country      | United States      |
	| State        | California         |
	| City         | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip          | 91765              |
	| Region       | US                 |
	| Language     | English            |
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Watcher" to the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| ZENOSBA |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Zen OSB Automotive |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View no project and user sync after role updates
	Customer role updates should not be reflected in Zendesk if customers and their respective organizations are not part of Zendesk.

	When I update a customer on the project with the code "ZENOSBA" with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the role of "Watcher"
	And I update a customer on the project with the code "ZENOSBA" with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the role of "Developer"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View no project and user sync after customer removal
	Customer removal updates should not be reflected in Zendesk if customers and their respective organizations are not part of Zendesk.

	When I remove a user the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer from the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View no project and user sync after watcher removal
	Watcher removal updates should not be reflected in Zendesk if customers and their respective organizations are not part of Zendesk.

	When I remove a user the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer from the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com